    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d74">

                <pb facs="0096" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/1721</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="72" xml:id="d74-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-05-24">May 24, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On your return to the office you will wish to give consideration to the
                    Department’s position on the question of the transfer of eight naval vessels to
                    China.</p>
                <p>I have asked Mr. Grew to analyze the matter thoroughly with the Navy and he will
                    be fully informed and prepared to discuss the matter with you at your
                    convenience.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E[<hi rendition="#small-caps">dward</hi>] S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >tettinius</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d74-f1" n="72" type="source" xml:id="d74-f1-content">
                <p>Marginal notation by the Secretary of State: “Why not consider lending first—in
                    view of trouble about Italian transfers. C[ordell] H[ull].”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
